  "body": "### Summary\nAs a reader who clears favourites with \"Lu\", I want the topic marked read on the forum too, so that it does not come back unread after a refresh, a relaunch or on another device.\n\nMilestone: M4 (operator, 2026-11-08). Found by the `2440d79..2fe43da3` sweep of #655.\n\n### Legacy @ `2fe43da3` (`legacy/duo-inner-cover`, AGENTS.md §2)\n- `96336bc9` \"Sync read state for favorite topics\": \"Lu\" removes the row at once and calls `markTopicRead`, which GETs the topic's last-page URL in the session (`HFRswift/Swift/Favorites.swift:33, 44-47, 102-115`; menu entries `1145`, `1192`). At `2440d79` \"Lu\" was local only (GAP-034).\n\n### Current SwiftHFR\n`TopicListModel.markRead` only records `markedRead` locally (`App/SwiftHFR/Navigation/TopicListModel+RowActions.swift:28-32`); LOT-125 (#216) and GAP-034 say \"Lu local only\".\n\n### Scope\n- \"Lu\" fetches the topic's last page with the account's session (the URL legacy builds), keeping the row's \"Annuler\" (GAP-034 b).\n- No HFR behaviour beyond the legacy code is assumed: that a last-page GET moves the flag is legacy's assumption; confirm it with a capture (before/after list) before relying on it in tests, or mark it *pending capture*.\n- Update LOT-125's spec and GAP-034 through the steward (#620).\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- After \"Lu\" and a list refresh, the topic is no longer unread on the forum (capture or Mac check).\n- A failed fetch keeps the local state and says nothing alarming; no write is sent (a GET only).\n- Tests use the loopback session (`hosts: .exactHost`).",
